# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Understand the packaging changes that occurred with the release of Qiskit "
"v1.0"
msgstr "Memahami perubahan pengemasan yang terjadi dengan rilis Qiskit v1.0"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Understand the breaking package changes"
msgstr "Memahami perubahan paket yang merusak kompatibilitas"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Understand the breaking package changes {#understand-the-breaking-package-"
"changes}"
msgstr ""
"Memahami perubahan paket Qiskit v1.0 yang merusak kompatibilitas "
"{#understand-the-breaking-package-changes}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Qiskit v1.0 uses a different packaging structure than previous Qiskit "
"versions and will likely cause problems in environments that use packages "
"that are not ready for Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Qiskit v1.0 menggunakan struktur pengemasan yang berbeda dari versi Qiskit "
"sebelumnya dan kemungkinan besar akan menyebabkan masalah di lingkungan yang"
" menggunakan paket yang belum siap untuk Qiskit v1.0.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Do not try to upgrade an existing Python virtual environment to Qiskit v1.0 in-place. \n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Jangan mencoba mengupgrade lingkungan virtual Python yang sudah ada ke Qiskit v1.0 secara langsung.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We will not make similar breaking packaging changes in the future. This is a one-time event, at the release of Qiskit v1.0, specifically so that our packaging story will be as easy as possible in the future.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Kami tidak akan membuat perubahan pengemasan yang merusak kompatibilitas serupa di masa depan. Ini adalah kejadian satu kali, saat rilis Qiskit v1.0, khusus agar kisah pengemasan kami semudah mungkin di masa depan.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This page contains detailed information about the pre-1.0 Qiskit package and"
" why we made the breaking packaging changes.\n"
msgstr ""
"Halaman ini berisi informasi terperinci tentang paket Qiskit pra-1.0 dan "
"mengapa kami membuat perubahan pengemasan yang merusak kompatibilitas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We know that the change is inconvenient, but this restores Qiskit to the "
"simple package structure that most Python packages use, which will be easier"
" for users, developers, and library authors after the Qiskit v1.0 transition"
" is complete.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kami tahu bahwa perubahan ini merepotkan, tapi ini mengembalikan Qiskit ke "
"struktur paket sederhana yang digunakan oleh sebagian besar paket Python, "
"yang akan lebih mudah bagi pengguna, pengembang, dan penulis pustaka setelah"
" transisi Qiskit v1.0 selesai.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Preface: glossary of Python packaging terminology {#preface-glossary-of-"
"python-packaging-terminology}"
msgstr ""
"Pendahuluan: glosarium terminologi pengemasan Python {#preface-glossary-of-"
"python-packaging-terminology}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To better explain how the old Qiskit metapackage was structured and how that has changed with the release of Qiskit v1.0, below is a glossary of commonly used Python-packaging jargon. The following words have specific meanings that we'll use in this document.\n"
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"**Click to expand to read through this page's glossary**\">\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk menjelaskan lebih baik bagaimana metapaket Qiskit lama disusun dan bagaimana itu telah berubah dengan rilis Qiskit v1.0, di bawah ini adalah glosarium istilah pengemasan Python yang umum digunakan. Kata-kata berikut memiliki arti spesifik yang akan kita gunakan dalam dokumen ini.\n"
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"**Klik di sini untuk membaca glosarium halaman ini**\">\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "**module**: A single Python file.\n"
msgstr "**module**: Satu file Python.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**package**: A directory containing an `__init__.py` and other files or packages that Python can read.\n"
"This is the actual code as installed on your computer, and is what executes when you run `import something`.\n"
"Python considers any directory that is on the search path to be something you can import (and will import many additional items).\n"
msgstr ""
"**package**: Direktori yang berisi `__init__.py` dan file atau paket lain yang bisa dibaca Python.\n"
"Ini adalah kode aktual yang terinstal di komputermu, dan yang dieksekusi saat kamu menjalankan `import something`.\n"
"Python menganggap setiap direktori yang ada di search path sebagai sesuatu yang bisa diimpor (dan akan mengimpor banyak item tambahan).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  This is not the same object that you `pip install` (which is a "
"*distribution*), but typically what you `pip install` and what you `import` "
"have the same name.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Ini bukan objek yang sama yang kamu `pip install` (yang merupakan sebuah "
"*distribution*), tapi biasanya apa yang kamu `pip install` dan apa yang kamu"
" `import` memiliki nama yang sama.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**submodule**, **subpackage**: These are imprecise terms, but are commonly used.\n"
"The _sub_ part means \"contained inside a package\".\n"
"A submodule is a module and a subpackage is a package, but they are part of a larger package.\n"
msgstr ""
"**submodule**, **subpackage**: Ini adalah istilah yang tidak presisi, tapi umum digunakan.\n"
"Bagian _sub_ berarti \"terkandung di dalam sebuah package\".\n"
"Submodule adalah modul dan subpackage adalah paket, tapi keduanya merupakan bagian dari paket yang lebih besar.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**namespace package**: A package that can have submodules or subpackages installed into it by other _distributions_.\n"
"Critically, no one distribution contributing to a namespace package necessarily owns all the installed files, so it can be tricky to completely uninstall\n"
"or upgrade one.\n"
msgstr ""
"**namespace package**: Sebuah package yang dapat memiliki submodul atau subpackage yang diinstal ke dalamnya oleh _distribution_ lain.\n"
"Yang krusial, tidak ada satu distribution pun yang berkontribusi ke namespace package yang pasti memiliki semua file yang terinstal, sehingga bisa jadi sulit untuk menguninstall atau mengupgrade salah satunya secara menyeluruh.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**distribution**: The compressed Python files, data files, and metadata that are downloaded when you run `pip install something`.\n"
"Often, a distribution contains exactly one package and the metadata about how to install it (its requirements and so on), but this is not required.\n"
"A distribution can contain zero or more modules or packages.\n"
msgstr ""
"**distribution**: File Python terkompresi, file data, dan metadata yang diunduh saat kamu menjalankan `pip install something`.\n"
"Biasanya, sebuah distribution berisi tepat satu package dan metadata tentang cara menginstalnya (persyaratannya dan sebagainya), tapi ini tidak diwajibkan.\n"
"Sebuah distribution bisa berisi nol atau lebih modul atau paket.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  If you are familiar with \"package managers\" outside the context of "
"Python, such as `apt` from Debian/Ubuntu or Homebrew on macOS, then what "
"they call a \"package\", Python calls a distribution, and there is no exact "
"match for what Python calls a package.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Jika kamu familiar dengan \"package manager\" di luar konteks Python, "
"seperti `apt` dari Debian/Ubuntu atau Homebrew di macOS, maka apa yang "
"mereka sebut \"package\", Python menyebutnya distribution, dan tidak ada "
"padanan tepat untuk apa yang Python sebut sebagai package.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Most sources talking about Python packaging use the term _package_ to mean both distributions and packages, and you must refer to the context to understand what is meant.\n"
"  In general, if you `import` it, the source means \"package\", and if you `pip install` it, the source means \"distribution\".\n"
msgstr ""
"  Sebagian besar sumber yang membahas pengemasan Python menggunakan istilah _package_ untuk merujuk pada distribution maupun package, dan kamu harus merujuk pada konteksnya untuk memahami maksudnya.\n"
"  Secara umum, jika kamu `import` sesuatu, sumber itu berarti \"package\", dan jika kamu `pip install` sesuatu, sumber itu berarti \"distribution\".\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**search path**: When trying to `import something`, Python searches a predefined list of places for a module or package called `something`.\n"
"The list of places is the _search path_.\n"
"You can see and modify the search path in `sys.path`.\n"
msgstr ""
"**requirement**: Sebuah distribution berisi informasi tentang distribution lain yang dibutuhkannya saat diinstal.\n"
"Distribution lain yang diperlukan adalah sebuah _requirement_, dan package manager (biasanya `pip` atau `conda`) harus memastikan semua requirement diinstal dengan versi yang kompatibel.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* **requirement**: A distribution contains information on other distributions it depends on when installed.\n"
"  Any other distribution that is necessary is a _requirement_, and the package manager (usually `pip` or `conda`) should ensure that all requirements are installed with compatible versions.\n"
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Python is highly dynamic, and many complexities can arise; for example, it's"
" possible that a **module** or **package** does not correspond to files on "
"disk, or that they are compiled extensions.\n"
msgstr ""
"Python sangat dinamis, dan banyak kompleksitas bisa muncul; misalnya, "
"dimungkinkan bahwa sebuah **module** atau **package** tidak bersesuaian "
"dengan file di disk, atau bahwa mereka adalah ekstensi yang dikompilasi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The **search path** is not only a search over directories, but for this discussion, only files on disk are relevant.\n"
"Further complications aren't necessary to understand the problems described in this section, so you can use the model described above.\n"
msgstr ""
"**Search path** tidak hanya pencarian atas direktori, tapi untuk diskusi ini, hanya file di disk yang relevan.\n"
"Komplikasi lebih lanjut tidak diperlukan untuk memahami masalah yang dijelaskan di bagian ini, jadi kamu bisa menggunakan model yang dijelaskan di atas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The old Qiskit structure {#the-old-qiskit-structure}"
msgstr "Struktur Qiskit lama {#the-old-qiskit-structure}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Historically, Qiskit was comprised of many Python distributions: `qiskit-terra`, the compiler core; `qiskit-aer`, the high-performance simulator; the original IBM Quantum&reg; provider; and several now-obsolete packages providing particular exploratory algorithmic or experiment-running features.\n"
"For user ease, we also provided a Python distribution called `qiskit`, which contained no code of its own, but caused all the other components to be installed.\n"
"We called this the _metapackage_, by analogy to similar concepts in other package managers.\n"
"The code of the core of Qiskit lived in `qiskit-terra`, which owned the root of the Python package `qiskit`. In other words, `qiskit-terra` controlled what happened when you ran `import qiskit`.\n"
"Until Qiskit v1.0, the `qiskit` package was a namespace package and contained a second namespace package at `qiskit.providers`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara historis, Qiskit terdiri dari banyak distribusi Python: `qiskit-terra`, inti compiler; `qiskit-aer`, simulator berkinerja tinggi; provider IBM Quantum&reg; asli; dan beberapa paket yang sekarang sudah usang yang menyediakan fitur algoritmik eksploratoris atau eksekusi eksperimen tertentu.\n"
"Untuk kemudahan pengguna, kami juga menyediakan distribusi Python bernama `qiskit`, yang tidak mengandung kode sendiri, tapi menyebabkan semua komponen lain diinstal.\n"
"Kami menyebut ini _metapackage_, dengan analogi ke konsep serupa di package manager lain.\n"
"Kode inti Qiskit berada di `qiskit-terra`, yang memiliki root dari package Python `qiskit`. Dengan kata lain, `qiskit-terra` mengontrol apa yang terjadi saat kamu menjalankan `import qiskit`.\n"
"Sampai Qiskit v1.0, package `qiskit` adalah namespace package dan mengandung namespace package kedua di `qiskit.providers`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This organization caused us and our users quite a few problems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Organisasi ini menyebabkan cukup banyak masalah bagi kami dan pengguna "
"kami.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, downstream libraries that depended on Qiskit often only actually needed the compiler core, and did not require the rest of the large ecosystem that came with `pip install qiskit`.\n"
"They would therefore correctly specify their requirement as `qiskit-terra`.\n"
"However, when people tried to uninstall Qiskit by running `pip uninstall qiskit`, `pip` encountered problems:\n"
msgstr ""
"Misalnya, pustaka downstream yang bergantung pada Qiskit seringkali hanya benar-benar membutuhkan inti compiler, dan tidak memerlukan sisa ekosistem besar yang datang dengan `pip install qiskit`.\n"
"Mereka karena itu dengan benar menentukan requirement mereka sebagai `qiskit-terra`.\n"
"Namun, saat orang mencoba menguninstall Qiskit dengan menjalankan `pip uninstall qiskit`, `pip` mengalami masalah:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`pip` does not remove distributions that are now unused. So `pip uninstall "
"qiskit` did almost nothing; there was no code in the distribution, so no "
"code was removed.\n"
msgstr ""
"`pip` tidak menghapus distribusi yang sekarang tidak digunakan. Jadi `pip "
"uninstall qiskit` hampir tidak melakukan apa-apa; tidak ada kode dalam "
"distribusi, sehingga tidak ada kode yang dihapus.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Even if it were to remove code, many downstream distributions would remain "
"installed because they depended on `qiskit-terra`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bahkan jika menghapus kode, banyak distribusi downstream akan tetap "
"terinstal karena bergantung pada `qiskit-terra`.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Even if `qiskit-terra` was uninstalled, it might still leave an importable "
"`qiskit` directory with no usable code, because it was a namespace "
"package.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bahkan jika `qiskit-terra` diuninstall, mungkin masih meninggalkan direktori"
" `qiskit` yang bisa diimpor tanpa kode yang bisa digunakan, karena itu "
"adalah namespace package.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When installing or upgrading distributions with a `pip install` command, `pip` also does not take into account previous requirement resolutions.\n"
"Because there were two packages, upgrading a package that required `qiskit-terra` to be upgraded caused an invalid environment; `pip` upgraded `qiskit-terra` but left `qiskit` untouched.\n"
"It issued a warning on this and all subsequent `pip install` commands, but because nothing appeared broken, users typically ignored the warning, and `pip` did not raise an error status or forbid operations.\n"
msgstr ""
"Saat menginstal atau mengupgrade distribusi dengan perintah `pip install`, `pip` juga tidak memperhitungkan resolusi requirement sebelumnya.\n"
"Karena ada dua paket, mengupgrade paket yang mengharuskan `qiskit-terra` untuk diupgrade menyebabkan lingkungan yang tidak valid; `pip` mengupgrade `qiskit-terra` tapi membiarkan `qiskit` tidak berubah.\n"
"Ia mengeluarkan peringatan pada perintah `pip install` ini dan semua perintah selanjutnya, tapi karena tidak ada yang tampak rusak, pengguna biasanya mengabaikan peringatan tersebut, dan `pip` tidak menampilkan status error atau melarang operasi.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Over time, we removed elements from the `qiskit` metapackage until, starting with Qiskit v0.44, only `qiskit-terra` remains.\n"
"Of these components, `qiskit-aer` still exists and is actively updated, but it is now installed as a separate distribution.\n"
msgstr ""
"Seiring waktu, kami menghapus elemen dari metapackage `qiskit` hingga, mulai Qiskit v0.44, hanya `qiskit-terra` yang tersisa.\n"
"Dari komponen-komponen ini, `qiskit-aer` masih ada dan diperbarui secara aktif, tapi sekarang diinstal sebagai distribusi terpisah.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Similarly, we ever more strongly discouraged other libraries from using the namespace hooks.\n"
"We removed the last Qiskit use of the hooks in non-obsolete packages with the release of Qiskit Aer v0.11 and its new `qiskit_aer` Python package, although until Qiskit v1.0 we also forced the namespace path `qiskit.providers.aer` to work.\n"
"Starting with Qiskit v1.0, we have removed the ability for packages to extend any `qiskit` namespace. Thus, `pip uninstall` on the correct distribution in a valid environment now works as expected.\n"
msgstr ""
"Demikian pula, kami semakin kuat menganjurkan pustaka lain untuk tidak menggunakan namespace hooks.\n"
"Kami menghapus penggunaan hooks Qiskit terakhir di paket yang tidak usang dengan rilis Qiskit Aer v0.11 dan package Python `qiskit_aer` yang baru, meskipun sampai Qiskit v1.0 kami juga memaksakan jalur namespace `qiskit.providers.aer` agar tetap berfungsi.\n"
"Mulai Qiskit v1.0, kami telah menghapus kemampuan bagi paket untuk memperluas namespace `qiskit` mana pun. Dengan demikian, `pip uninstall` pada distribusi yang benar di lingkungan yang valid sekarang berfungsi seperti yang diharapkan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The new Qiskit structure {#the-new-qiskit-structure}"
msgstr "Struktur Qiskit baru {#the-new-qiskit-structure}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Starting with version 1.0, Qiskit comprises a single distribution, called `qiskit`, which installs one single package, also called `qiskit`, which owns all the code contained in its directory.\n"
"This is the normal structure of Python code, and is the simplest and least error-prone structure.\n"
msgstr ""
"Mulai versi 1.0, Qiskit terdiri dari satu distribusi, bernama `qiskit`, yang menginstal satu paket tunggal, juga bernama `qiskit`, yang memiliki semua kode yang terkandung dalam direktorinya.\n"
"Ini adalah struktur normal kode Python, dan merupakan struktur paling sederhana dan paling sedikit rentan terhadap error.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The `qiskit-terra` distribution on PyPI will never be updated to version 1.0 or beyond; it is entirely superseded by `qiskit`.\n"
"The name `qiskit-terra` is no longer involved in the installation.\n"
"However, the `qiskit-terra` package is not being removed from PyPI, and we will leave its most recent version in a working state, so old scientific code and legacy packages can more easily continue to use it.\n"
msgstr ""
"Distribusi `qiskit-terra` di PyPI tidak akan pernah diperbarui ke versi 1.0 atau lebih tinggi; itu sepenuhnya digantikan oleh `qiskit`.\n"
"Nama `qiskit-terra` tidak lagi terlibat dalam instalasi.\n"
"Namun, paket `qiskit-terra` tidak dihapus dari PyPI, dan kami akan membiarkan versi terbarunya dalam keadaan berfungsi, sehingga kode ilmiah lama dan paket legacy dapat lebih mudah terus menggunakannya.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, because of the metapackage legacy and deficiencies in `pip` as a package manager, it is not possible for us to make a completely smooth upgrade path for users to Qiskit v1.0, especially while some packages depend on earlier versions of Qiskit, and some require only Qiskit v1.0+.\n"
"These problems will lessen as more of the ecosystem migrates to Qiskit v1.0.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sayangnya, karena warisan metapackage dan kekurangan di `pip` sebagai package manager, tidak mungkin bagi kami untuk membuat jalur upgrade yang sepenuhnya mulus bagi pengguna ke Qiskit v1.0, terutama saat beberapa paket bergantung pada versi Qiskit yang lebih lama, dan beberapa hanya memerlukan Qiskit v1.0+.\n"
"Masalah-masalah ini akan berkurang seiring semakin banyak ekosistem yang bermigrasi ke Qiskit v1.0.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Where did the application modules go? {#where-did-the-application-modules-"
"go}"
msgstr "Ke mana modul aplikasi pergi? {#where-did-the-application-modules-go}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You may notice that the command `pip install qiskit` will no longer includes"
" packages such as `qiskit-aer` or `qiskit-nature`. With the removal of the "
"metapackage structure, many of these packages were split into distributions "
"that need to be installed separately.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kamu mungkin memperhatikan bahwa perintah `pip install qiskit` tidak lagi "
"menyertakan paket seperti `qiskit-aer` atau `qiskit-nature`. Dengan "
"penghapusan struktur metapackage, banyak paket ini dibagi menjadi distribusi"
" yang perlu diinstal secara terpisah.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before the release of the Qiskit SDK v1.0, Qiskit was comprised of many "
"different Python distributions, such as `qiskit-terra`, the compiler core; "
"`qiskit-aer`, the high-performance simulator; the original IBM Quantum&reg; "
"provider; and several now-obsolete packages providing particular exploratory"
" algorithmic or experiment-running features.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebelum rilis Qiskit SDK v1.0, Qiskit terdiri dari banyak distribusi Python "
"yang berbeda, seperti `qiskit-terra`, inti compiler; `qiskit-aer`, simulator"
" berkinerja tinggi; provider IBM Quantum&reg; asli; dan beberapa paket yang "
"sekarang sudah usang yang menyediakan fitur algoritmik eksploratoris atau "
"eksekusi eksperimen tertentu.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you want to install the packages that were previously included in the "
"Qiskit metapackage, visit the [Qiskit "
"ecosystem](https://www.ibm.com/quantum/ecosystem) to find a range of "
